 {'idx': 11, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'The U.S. Agency for International Development (USAID), an independent agency under the Department of State established in place of the Marshall Plan for the purpose of determining and distributing foreign aid, does not use the term Near East. Its definition of Middle East corresponds to that of the State Department, which officially prefers the term Near East.', 'title': 'Near East'}
