 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Tiffany Blue is the colloquial name for the light medium robin egg blue color associated with Tiffany & Co., the New York City jewelry company created by Charles Tiffany and John Young in 1837. The color was used on the cover of Tiffany\'s "Blue Book", first published in 1845. Since then, Tiffany & Co. has used the color extensively on promotional materials like boxes and bags.', 'title': 'Tiffany Blue'}
 {'idx': 8, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "In the original Broadway production, ``Some Enchanted Evening ''was sung by former Metropolitan Opera bass Ezio Pinza. Pinza won the Tony Award for Best Actor in 1950 for this role, and the song made him a favorite with audiences and listeners who normally did not attend or listen to opera. In the 2001 London revival of the show, Philip Quast won an Olivier Award for Best Actor for his role as Emile, and seven years later, international opera singer Paulo Szot won a Tony for his portrayal in the 2008 New York revival.", 'title': 'Some Enchanted Evening'}
