 {'idx': 2, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Silver How is a fell in the English Lake District, standing over the village of Grasmere. How, derived from the Old Norse word "haugr", is a common local term for a hill or mound.', 'title': 'Silver How'}
 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "``Das Lied der Deutschen ''English: The Song of the Germans Facsimile of Hoffmann von Fallersleben's manuscript of`` Das Lied der Deutschen'' National anthem of Germany (only the 3rd verse) Former national anthem of West Germany (only the 3rd verse was sung on official occasions) Also known as ``Deutschlandlied ''English: The Song of Germany Lyrics August Heinrich Hoffmann von Fallersleben, 1841 Music Joseph Haydn, 1797 Adopted 1922 Audio sample`` Deutschlandlied'' (all verses) file help", 'title': 'Deutschlandlied'}
